1
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:53,020
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,800
[Episode 1]

3
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,050
Hello? Hello?

4
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:21,780
Hello!

5
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:23,060
Stop yelling into the phone.

6
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:24,400
The line must've burned out by now.

7
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:25,530
Hurry up and pack your things.

8
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:26,770
Head down along the railway.

9
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,660
We might run into a rescue team. Hurry.

10
00:01:30,010 --> 00:01:30,370
Liu Yang.

11
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:31,230
What?

12
00:01:33,729 --> 00:01:35,060
Come with me to the tool room.

13
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:36,200
We need to find some headlamps.

14
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,000
Come on, let's go.

15
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:41,759
Give me the flashlight.

16
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:42,810
I'll light the way for you.

17
00:01:42,810 --> 00:01:43,920
Hurry. Look for it.

18
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:45,650
Over there. There, there, there.

19
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:48,280
Find some extra batteries.

20
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:56,400
Hurry.

21
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,000
I'm sorry, man.

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,250
I've got a wife and kids.

23
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,730
You don't have anyone.

24
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:16,460
Every wrong has its source,
and every debt has its debtor.

25
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,930
If you become a ghost,
don't come after us.

26
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:23,280
It was Zhao Changyou who wanted you dead.

27
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,150
We had nothing to do with it.

28
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:28,410
Bro,

29
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:29,490
we gotta go.

30
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,560
The fire's coming this way.

31
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:41,660
[Tool Room]

32
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:38,690
How is it?

33
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:41,579
Let's go. Hurry.

34
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,930
[Tool Room]

35
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:03,630
Zhao Changyou took the buyer's deposit

36
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:05,440
and has been hounding us
to ship the goods every day.

37
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:07,890
That bastard secretly reported us
to the railway depot.

38
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,920
It's been six months,

39
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,280
and we haven't managed
to move a single shipment.

40
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,360
We're risking our lives doing this.

41
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,040
We can't let that bastard
screw everything up.

42
00:03:14,210 --> 00:03:15,230
He got what he deserved.

43
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:16,960
This fire is Heaven's will.

44
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,310
What about our shipment?

45
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:41,630
What if it gets burned in the cave?

46
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:42,780
The goods are worth a lot.

47
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,860
Why don't we take a few with us?

48
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,250
I've sealed the cave entrance.

49
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,360
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

50
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:48,430
Bro,

51
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:51,000
what if the forest firefighters
find the goods?

52
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,840
Pin it all on Liu Yang.

53
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:53,930
He's dead.
No one can testify against us now.

54
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:55,400
Maodan.

55
00:03:56,090 --> 00:03:56,530
I...

56
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,090
Where is Maodan?

57
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,060
-He was just here.
-Maodan!

58
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,010
Maodan!

59
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:05,000
Maodan!

60
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:25,040
Maodan!

61
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,190
Maodan!

62
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,220
Maodan!

63
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:32,630
Maodan!

64
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,270
Maodan!

65
00:04:35,330 --> 00:04:36,010
Maodan!

66
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,630
-Maodan!
-Maodan!

67
00:04:39,270 --> 00:04:40,159
Maodan!

68
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,159
Maodan!

69
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:52,180
Run!

70
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:53,550
Go, go, go.

71
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:54,310
Go, go, go.

72
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:10,160
Who is it?

73
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:19,110
♪ The snow weighs down the grave mound,
and joss paper flies ♪

74
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:22,770
♪ Icicles hang down
around the neck and spine ♪

75
00:07:20,670 --> 00:07:25,010
[Tiecheng, 1998]

76
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:25,870
♪ The drumhead thumps,
and living ghosts leap ♪

77
00:07:25,010 --> 00:07:26,610
[Shasha Hair Salon]

78
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:29,540
♪ Blood foam splashes
across the frozen earth ♪

79
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:33,159
♪ The north wind sweeps in,
carrying a baby's shrill laughter ♪

80
00:07:33,159 --> 00:07:36,830
♪ The umbilical cord coils
round copper coins ♪

81
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:40,920
♪ It foretells that your life this time
won't last long ♪

82
00:07:39,390 --> 00:07:42,909
[The Soul-Guiding Banner of...]

83
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:44,570
♪ The chain of retribution crawls
across the frozen ground ♪

84
00:07:44,570 --> 00:07:48,250
♪ Wraps round your ankles,
where ice flowers abound ♪

85
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:51,860
♪ The noose you buried years ago ♪

86
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:54,920
♪ Has come right back
around your own neck ♪

87
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:58,120
♪ So stew your heart and liver
to warm the wine ♪

88
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:01,270
♪ Repay your debt to the dead,
then be reborn ♪

89
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:33,940
I am the Yellow Immortal
of White Mountain.

90
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,740
Who is it?

91
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:38,370
Who summoned me?

92
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,720
I-I did.

93
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:41,940
Help me.

94
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:42,860
You.

95
00:08:46,550 --> 00:08:47,770
There are three of them.

96
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:48,790
Two men

97
00:08:49,270 --> 00:08:50,170
and a woman.

98
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,220
One has an arm

99
00:08:52,710 --> 00:08:54,180
around your neck.

100
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,120
Another has an arm around your waist.

101
00:08:57,170 --> 00:08:58,390
And the third

102
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,320
has a hold of your leg.

103
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:04,740
Great Immortal,

104
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:05,870
save me.

105
00:09:06,010 --> 00:09:07,580
Great Immortal, save me.

106
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:09,440
Save me. Please, save me.

107
00:09:09,770 --> 00:09:10,240
Save me.

108
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,460
I shall summon the Heavenly Soldiers

109
00:09:12,870 --> 00:09:15,010
to drive away these 3 evil spirits.

110
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:15,620
Okay.

111
00:09:22,410 --> 00:09:23,460
Remember:

112
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:31,940
don't make any sudden moves.

113
00:09:32,790 --> 00:09:34,240
You must not open your eyes.

114
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:34,790
Okay.

115
00:09:34,790 --> 00:09:36,060
Keep your eyes shut.

116
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,340
They're shut.

117
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,080
Don't anger the Heavenly Soldiers.

118
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:42,050
Heavenly Soldiers, come quickly!

119
00:09:42,050 --> 00:09:43,180
They're coming.

120
00:09:43,370 --> 00:09:45,240
Heavenly Soldiers, come quickly!

121
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,200
Heavenly Soldiers are here!

122
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,870
-The Heavenly Soldiers are coming.
-Heavenly Soldiers, come quickly!

123
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:49,030
Come on.

124
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:50,050
Don't move!

125
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,120
Police! Don't move!

126
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,010
What's your name?

127
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:55,960
What's your name?

128
00:09:56,910 --> 00:09:57,890
Liu Xiang?

129
00:09:58,390 --> 00:09:59,200
Is that right?

130
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:01,740
Take him away!

131
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:05,340
This guy's been breaking into homes
and robbing people all over the place.

132
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:06,530
The money he offered
as offerings was all stolen.

133
00:10:06,530 --> 00:10:07,860
Wouldn't he be afraid
of offending the Great Immortal?

134
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:08,940
The Great Immortal must've been offended.

135
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,180
Otherwise, how else would we
have caught him here?

136
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:12,160
Juan.

137
00:10:12,190 --> 00:10:13,330
You really outdid yourself this time.

138
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:14,670
You earned yourself some serious merit.

139
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:15,380
Really?

140
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,030
I'm telling you, it wore me out.

141
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:18,860
I've never been good
at memorizing passages since I was a kid.

142
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:20,360
That invocation chant was so hard.

143
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,630
I couldn't sleep for several nights.

144
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:22,860
I could only memorize two lines.

145
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:23,820
Everything after that
was just me making things up.

146
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:24,630
I was so afraid I'd be found out.

147
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:25,890
Seriously? You were making it up?

148
00:10:25,890 --> 00:10:26,610
I really was!

149
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,940
You made it look so convincing.

150
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:28,590
Really?

151
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:29,870
I've got some talent, don't I?

152
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:30,910
You've got a ton of talent.

153
00:10:30,910 --> 00:10:31,500
My heart was pounding

154
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,470
when I first started performing.

155
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:33,170
I was so nervous.

156
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:35,130
I'll take him back and question him first.

157
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:36,050
Then we'll chat later.

158
00:10:36,050 --> 00:10:36,820
Sure, we'll chat later.

159
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:37,360
Thanks.

160
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:38,850
Don't mention it.

161
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:40,290
W-We'll chat back at the station.

162
00:10:40,290 --> 00:10:41,530
Sure. I'll buy you a meal sometime.

163
00:10:41,530 --> 00:10:42,200
Okay. Let's go, let's go.

164
00:10:46,050 --> 00:10:49,860
♪ Blood foam splashes
across the frozen earth ♪

165
00:10:50,130 --> 00:10:52,150
♪ The north wind sweeps in,
carrying a baby's shrill laughter ♪

166
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:53,830
Juan, why are you still singing?

167
00:10:54,170 --> 00:10:56,050
You're really something.

168
00:10:56,050 --> 00:10:56,670
Am I?

169
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,270
Come on,
drive away some evil spirits for me.

170
00:10:58,270 --> 00:10:59,940
Don't let that outfit go to waste.
Come on.

171
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:01,410
I think you've got some evil spirits
on you.

172
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:02,980
Otherwise, why would your partner
have dumped you?

173
00:11:05,170 --> 00:11:06,370
Why do you have to say things

174
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:08,130
that cut so deep?

175
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:09,500
What? Isn't it true?

176
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:12,790
Quit eating other people's stuff.

177
00:11:12,790 --> 00:11:14,290
How can you just keep eating like that?

178
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:16,740
These aren't offerings, are they?

179
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:21,100
Well... that's not right.

180
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,130
Let's put them back where they were.

181
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:24,980
It's fine.

182
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:26,860
What's fine?

183
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,120
You never get tired
of taking advantage of people.

184
00:11:28,470 --> 00:11:32,470
[Yuhong Stadium]

185
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,370
It's not like I'm trying to hurt you.

186
00:11:31,370 --> 00:11:32,110
Love

187
00:11:32,110 --> 00:11:33,010
is a fugitive too.

188
00:11:33,290 --> 00:11:34,750
It fools around with you here today,

189
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:36,200
then tomorrow,
you don't know where it's gone.

190
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:37,860
If it's not yours, you can't make it stay.

191
00:11:37,860 --> 00:11:39,290
If it is yours, seize the moment.

192
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:40,620
Pin it down and don't let it get away.

193
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,170
Just like that guy today.

194
00:11:40,730 --> 00:11:48,550
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

195
00:11:42,290 --> 00:11:44,340
He committed so many crimes
all over Tiecheng.

196
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,440
So how did we happen to catch him

197
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,600
at Yuhong Square?

198
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,650
That's just his fate.

199
00:11:48,650 --> 00:11:49,890
You're not even married.

200
00:11:49,890 --> 00:11:50,790
You're just dating.

201
00:11:51,530 --> 00:11:52,600
So what if you break up?

202
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,100
Don't go around
looking so miserable all the time.

203
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,370
I've been married for 7 years.

204
00:11:55,370 --> 00:11:56,980
That bastard went to Guangzhou
to make his fortune.

205
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:58,300
He found himself some floozy over there.

206
00:11:58,410 --> 00:11:59,590
Then he came back and wanted a divorce.

207
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:01,420
So what? Did I lose anything?

208
00:12:02,650 --> 00:12:03,930
As if I'm scared of him.

209
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:05,960
I'll find you someone else later.

210
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:06,550
It's okay.

211
00:12:07,050 --> 00:12:08,840
Don't worry about it.

212
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,050
You should hurry up
and find a new husband.

213
00:12:11,050 --> 00:12:12,500
What are you gonna do when you get old?

214
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,000
It's better to rely on yourself
than on a man.

215
00:12:15,290 --> 00:12:16,650
I've definitely earned
some merit this time.

216
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,700
When I report it to the bureau
at the end of the year,

217
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,650
I'll surely get promoted
to some position or other.

218
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:22,910
It'd be best if I could get transferred
back to the branch bureau.

219
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,440
At the very least,
I could work in logistics.

220
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,890
Anything's better
than patrolling around here.

221
00:12:45,790 --> 00:12:48,500
Don't you think
it's unusually cold this year

222
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:50,410
compared to previous years?

223
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:55,130
Do you know why?

224
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:58,360
Because this year

225
00:12:58,740 --> 00:12:59,750
is the Year of the Earth Tiger.

226
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:01,620
The Heavenly Stem belongs to Earth,

227
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:03,500
and it's the white tiger
returning to the mountains.

228
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:04,620
It's dangerous.

229
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:06,260
Still trying to fool people
at the police station?

230
00:13:06,890 --> 00:13:07,670
Let her go.

231
00:13:07,670 --> 00:13:08,580
She's been cleared of suspicion.

232
00:13:09,030 --> 00:13:09,820
See?

233
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:10,740
I forgot about you.

234
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:11,740
Your legs must've gone numb
from squatting all this time.

235
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:12,980
Juan, I'm gonna go inside
and catch a quick nap.

236
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:13,530
Go ahead.

237
00:13:13,530 --> 00:13:14,670
You're on night duty tonight.
Don't forget.

238
00:13:14,670 --> 00:13:15,170
Okay.

239
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:16,550
How's it going?

240
00:13:18,430 --> 00:13:19,280
Pretty good.

241
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:21,370
That radiator's been

242
00:13:21,370 --> 00:13:22,240
roasting me so much.

243
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:24,000
It dried out my rheumatism.

244
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:24,780
Really?

245
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,620
Then enjoy it for a while longer.

246
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:27,240
Okay.

247
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,670
How is it? Did you catch the guy?

248
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:33,340
What does it have to do with you?

249
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:34,940
Here, have some.

250
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:35,580
Be serious.

251
00:13:39,030 --> 00:13:40,050
Wan Xiuhua.

252
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:41,360
I'm not trying to lecture you,

253
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:43,630
but Yuhong Square is only so big.

254
00:13:44,650 --> 00:13:47,030
Your store is right
in front of the police station.

255
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:48,740
How can you not run an honest business?

256
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,050
How am I not running an honest business?

257
00:13:50,050 --> 00:13:51,320
Do you really run an honest business?

258
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:52,530
How much more honest can I be?

259
00:13:52,530 --> 00:13:53,740
At my funeral store,

260
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,360
when someone dies...

261
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:57,550
What are you doing?

262
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,620
Let's say someone dies.

263
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,590
They come to your place first to cancel
their household registration, right?

264
00:14:02,670 --> 00:14:03,650
Then they walk out the door

265
00:14:04,170 --> 00:14:05,030
and come to my place.

266
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,790
I handle everything
from funeral arrangements

267
00:14:06,790 --> 00:14:08,410
and rites for the dead to summoning
and sending off spirits.

268
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,750
I've got the whole package.

269
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,220
Isn't that just perfect?

270
00:14:12,250 --> 00:14:13,400
Cut it out

271
00:14:13,550 --> 00:14:14,630
with all that spooky nonsense.

272
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:18,270
I'm only letting you off because we went
to elementary school together.

273
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,050
How many times have I
warned and lectured you?

274
00:14:20,050 --> 00:14:21,410
Don't you know that yourself?

275
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:25,360
You may not believe in it,
but some people do.

276
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:26,150
Who?

277
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:29,340
The more guilty a person is,

278
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,480
the more afraid they are of retribution.

279
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:32,960
The guy from yesterday? I could tell

280
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:34,720
right away something was off
when he walked in.

281
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:36,740
He had a debt on his conscience.

282
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,170
Scary, huh?

283
00:14:40,530 --> 00:14:42,820
You really will take money
from anyone, won't you?

284
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,440
Good thing he was a robber.

285
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:47,290
If he'd been a murderer,

286
00:14:47,290 --> 00:14:48,550
wouldn't he have killed you
to silence you?

287
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,840
He wouldn't dare.

288
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,120
The police station is right
across the way.

289
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:55,980
If anything really happened to me,

290
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:57,200
I'd just let out one good yell.

291
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,620
Wouldn't you all come running over?

292
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:00,940
Well, you're not so dumb after all.

293
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,740
You know the people's police are
more reliable than any Great Immortal.

294
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:03,530
You bet.

295
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:09,480
What are you looking around for?

296
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,240
There are only a few of us here.

297
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,270
Come closer. Come closer.

298
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:12,050
What?

299
00:15:12,410 --> 00:15:12,910
Hey—

300
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:14,100
just talk normally, okay?

301
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,340
Last night,

302
00:15:18,670 --> 00:15:20,480
the Yellow Immortal
appeared to me in a dream.

303
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,440
It said Yuhong Square

304
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:24,360
is basically a giant incense burner,

305
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,550
and it's going to use

306
00:15:28,170 --> 00:15:28,860
three human lives as incense.

307
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:29,740
Cut the crap.

308
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:30,360
I don't believe

309
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,600
a word of your nonsense.

310
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,320
What was all that stuff you were
telling me at the beginning of the year?

311
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,480
"Juanzi, I've read your fortune.

312
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,700
You're going to have a lucky year.

313
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:37,840
Your fortune is great,

314
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:38,700
and a benefactor is entering your life."

315
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,500
What now?
It's already the end of the year.

316
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,410
Aren't I still stuck with an empty home

317
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:43,240
and a lonely bed?

318
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:44,740
With your lousy fortune-telling skills,

319
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:45,780
you call yourself a fortune teller?

320
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:46,670
Why don't you tell me

321
00:15:46,670 --> 00:15:47,840
how much a pound of Chinese cabbage
will cost tomorrow,

322
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,500
and leave it at that?

323
00:15:49,410 --> 00:15:50,950
Don't worry.

324
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:53,530
What I predicted for you still counts
until the Beginning of Spring.

325
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:55,550
What?

326
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:57,270
Pick someone up?

327
00:15:57,860 --> 00:15:58,630
Yeah, that's right.

328
00:15:58,910 --> 00:16:00,290
She asked for you by name.

329
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:02,750
Who is it?

330
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,840
Put her on the phone.

331
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:09,510
She... can't come to the phone.

332
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:11,080
She's mute?

333
00:16:13,050 --> 00:16:14,050
No, Juan.

334
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,790
Look, just come over here
as soon as you can.

335
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:16,940
Okay.

336
00:16:58,340 --> 00:16:59,150
What are you looking at?

337
00:17:00,550 --> 00:17:01,330
No, man.

338
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:02,600
I'm just saying your shoelace is undone.

339
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:23,710
[No Entry]
